Question Title: Simplify the Compilation Process

Question Link:
https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/9kh4giios2j4?lecture_hash=t5qc0u6ap8tg

Solution:
echo "#!bin/bash" > build.sh
echo "gcc hello.c -o hello" >> build.sh
chmod +x build.sh
gcc hello.c -o hello
./build.sh
./hello

Approach:
1. write the shebang in the build.sh file
2. compile hello.c into an executable hello
3. execute build.sh and hello

Result:
Hello from C gets printed